509	The diffs to the model that are now possible, each for your word:
510	- `^T` declared in the helper file's api, so that lines 21 to 24 leave the model;
511	- `(onehot(ids, vocabSize))^T dX` in line 70;
512	- `SUM[j <- 0#i] matCount(j)` in line 43, without the type;
513	- `∑` for `SUM` in lines 28, 43 and 52;
514	- the two tables in lines 37 to 41, in the interpreter only;
515	- the sized vector functions, which belong to your parked decision on static sizes.
516	
517	Three events to know.
518	- **The machine restarted at 01:26.** Two workers were lost while they waited for a long test. The run was resumed two minutes later, and two new workers finished their tasks from what was on disk. No work was lost. It cost 0.22 million tokens and about a quarter of an hour.
519	- **Your chat question about the Fortify output reached five workers.** The tool that runs a batch puts the message that started the coordinator's turn in front of each worker's instructions, and tells the worker that it outranks them. Two workers wrote that they could not answer it, and two searched the tree for it. Nothing else followed. An instruction in that place would have been obeyed, so I propose that a batch is launched only from a turn that no message of yours started.
520	- **The coordinating session did not commit while the batch merged its tasks.** The slip of the batch before did not recur.
521	
522	The cost, in tokens written:
523	- the landing work of batch 30: 7.63 million in its span, of which the landing itself was 3.88 million;
524	- the preparation of this batch: 6.35 million in its span, of which the plan, its two checks and the join of the two moved tasks were 1.12 million;
525	- the run: 7.54 million in its span, 5.00 million by its own agents, against the plan's 6.2 million, in 6 h 10 min against 10 hours.
526	
527	Fifteen of the sixteen workers that were given a briefing read all of it within 80 seconds. The one that did not took over a finished task after the restart.
528	
529	For the next batch, 31: its tasks all edit the code generator's main file, where this batch landed one change, so one task's line numbers move. Its base build must be made new. Six of the new defects fit it. It is not launched before you have dealt with the post-mortem of 16 November.
